1
00:00:54,526 --> 00:00:57,942
Remember when they let
commercial airlines land in this town?

2
00:00:58,029 --> 00:01:00,271
I don't understand where we're going...

3
00:01:00,365 --> 00:01:02,523
...or why we're bothering anyhow.

4
00:01:02,701 --> 00:01:05,737
-You're doing a good deed.
-Give us a better reason.

5
00:01:06,163 --> 00:01:09,994
A maniac hijacked a municipal bus
with 30 passengers on it.

6
00:01:10,458 --> 00:01:13,958
I got a hunch where those passengers are
and who that maniac is.

7
00:01:14,045 --> 00:01:15,456
Share it with us.

8
00:01:16,089 --> 00:01:17,120
Phoenix.

9
00:01:17,716 --> 00:01:18,961
Simon Phoenix.

10
00:01:56,212 --> 00:01:58,252
Send a maniac to catch one.

11
00:02:00,591 --> 00:02:01,587
Phoenix!

12
00:03:14,248 --> 00:03:15,991
Don't move, Phoenix.

13
00:03:19,586 --> 00:03:21,128
You're under arrest.

14
00:03:21,797 --> 00:03:23,339
Arrest? Shit.

15
00:03:24,132 --> 00:03:25,840
And you're trespassing.

16
00:03:27,177 --> 00:03:28,588
Where are the passengers?

17
00:03:28,678 --> 00:03:30,718
Oh, yes, the passengers.

18
00:03:30,889 --> 00:03:32,431
Well, they're....

19
00:03:33,517 --> 00:03:34,762
Fuck you.

20
00:03:34,851 --> 00:03:36,725
The passengers are gone.

21
00:03:37,187 --> 00:03:40,686
See, I told the city,
"Look, nobody comes down here."

22
00:03:41,316 --> 00:03:43,024
Postmen figured it out...

23
00:03:43,193 --> 00:03:44,770
...policemen figured it out.

24
00:03:44,861 --> 00:03:48,147
But the goddamn bus drivers
just wouldn't listen.

25
00:03:48,782 --> 00:03:50,573
Last time, Phoenix.

26
00:03:50,951 --> 00:03:52,943
Where are the hostages?

27
00:03:53,078 --> 00:03:56,328
To hell with the hostages!.
This is between you and me!.

28
00:04:01,211 --> 00:04:02,290
What you got?

29
00:04:02,378 --> 00:04:03,458
Do something.

30
00:04:03,546 --> 00:04:04,827
Go ahead.

31
00:04:05,799 --> 00:04:07,957
You're up to your ass in gasoline.

32
00:04:11,346 --> 00:04:13,219
I'll set your ass on fire.

33
00:04:26,361 --> 00:04:27,938
Is it cold in here...

34
00:04:28,696 --> 00:04:30,238
...or is it just me?

35
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:03,938
Where are they, Phoenix?

36
00:05:04,023 --> 00:05:05,766
Now, where did I put them?

37
00:05:06,066 --> 00:05:09,317
I swear, I'd lose my head
if it wasn't attached.

38
00:05:10,654 --> 00:05:12,647
I'll keep that in mind.

39
00:05:54,197 --> 00:05:57,364
Damn it, I'm tired
of this "demolition-man" shit!

40
00:05:57,826 --> 00:06:00,068
You were not supposed
to come down here!

41
00:06:00,162 --> 00:06:03,744
You were not supposed to attempt
the arrest of Phoenix alone...

42
00:06:03,999 --> 00:06:05,493
...or to blow anything up!

43
00:06:05,584 --> 00:06:08,750
It wasn't me! He dumped the gas
and rigged the place to blow!

44
00:06:08,837 --> 00:06:10,497
Right, you weren't involved.

45
00:06:10,589 --> 00:06:13,210
I know you've tried
to nail this psycho for years.

46
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:15,257
But remember a thing called...

47
00:06:15,427 --> 00:06:17,170
...official police procedure?

48
00:06:17,262 --> 00:06:19,219
-Where are the hostages?
-They're not here.

49
00:06:19,306 --> 00:06:20,005
What?

50
00:06:20,098 --> 00:06:22,007
He must've stashed them someplace else!

51
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:23,974
Are you sure they weren't in there?

52
00:06:24,060 --> 00:06:27,595
I did a thermo check and there were eight
of them, all part of his gang.

53
00:06:27,689 --> 00:06:28,851
Wrong again!

54
00:06:29,024 --> 00:06:30,767
You got something to say?

55
00:06:31,693 --> 00:06:33,235
Get him out of here!

56
00:06:34,028 --> 00:06:35,060
Motherfucker!

57
00:06:35,155 --> 00:06:37,396
We are going to have a chat.

58
00:06:38,283 --> 00:06:39,278
Captain!

59
00:06:40,285 --> 00:06:42,740
Over here! There're bodies everywhere!

60
00:06:42,871 --> 00:06:44,413
There must be 20 or 30.

61
00:06:44,497 --> 00:06:45,991
They're everywhere.

62
00:06:47,375 --> 00:06:48,786
See that? I told him!

63
00:06:48,876 --> 00:06:50,703
He said he didn't care!

64
00:06:51,004 --> 00:06:54,752
How could you sacrifice
all those innocent people for me!

65
00:06:55,508 --> 00:06:57,299
What kind of man are you?

66
00:06:57,385 --> 00:07:00,718
We'll spend a lot of quality time together.
'Bye, sweetie!

67
00:07:00,805 --> 00:07:02,347
Honey! Sugar!

68
00:07:03,391 --> 00:07:05,716
If you got a lawyer, better call him.

69
00:08:02,074 --> 00:08:05,657
John Spartan, you've done great deeds
for Los Angeles.

70
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:09,370
So, it is with some regret that l,
William Smithers...

71
00:08:09,498 --> 00:08:13,033
...acting as Assistant Warden,
hereby carry out this sentence.

72
00:08:13,293 --> 00:08:14,574
Skip it.

73
00:08:15,629 --> 00:08:17,787
You've been sentenced to 70 years...

74
00:08:17,881 --> 00:08:22,128
...sub-zero re-habilitation
in the California Cryo-Penitentiary...

75
00:08:22,427 --> 00:08:25,796
...for the involuntary manslaughter
of 30 civilians.

76
00:08:26,181 --> 00:08:27,344
Skip it.

77
00:08:27,474 --> 00:08:30,890
You'll be placed in cryo-stasis
for the duration of your sentence...

78
00:08:30,977 --> 00:08:34,512
...and your behavior will be altered
through synaptic suggestion.

79
00:08:34,606 --> 00:08:38,057
You'll be eligible for parole
no earlier than the year 2046.

80
00:08:46,993 --> 00:08:48,108
I'm sorry.

81
00:11:50,925 --> 00:11:52,254
All personnel...

82
00:11:52,343 --> 00:11:55,961
...the next scheduled parole hearing
for prisoner Gilmour...

83
00:11:56,097 --> 00:11:58,137
...will take place at 07:. 15.

84
00:11:59,434 --> 00:12:03,266
Warden William Smithers
report to Level A, conference room.

85
00:12:09,610 --> 00:12:11,021
Mellow greetings.

86
00:12:11,696 --> 00:12:14,234
Be well, Lieutenant Lenina Huxley.

87
00:12:15,116 --> 00:12:16,943
As it is a beautiful...

88
00:12:17,118 --> 00:12:20,818
...Monday morning and as my duty log
irrationally requires it...

89
00:12:20,997 --> 00:12:23,666
...I'm querying you
on the prison population.

90
00:12:23,749 --> 00:12:25,493
Does the tedium continue?

91
00:12:25,626 --> 00:12:28,331
Your question is amusing but irrelevant.

92
00:12:28,462 --> 00:12:31,132
The prisoners are ice cubes.
They never move.

93
00:12:31,841 --> 00:12:34,925
I find this lack of stimulus
to be truly disappointing.

94
00:12:35,011 --> 00:12:36,754
-Don't you think?
-I try not to.

95
00:12:36,846 --> 00:12:39,171
You're young, think all you want.

96
00:12:39,348 --> 00:12:42,384
Things don't happen anymore,
we've taken care of all that.

97
00:12:42,476 --> 00:12:45,311
I'll fiber-op you back
after the parole hearings.

98
00:12:45,396 --> 00:12:46,973
Have a peachy day.

99
00:12:47,148 --> 00:12:48,179
Be well.

100
00:12:48,357 --> 00:12:49,222
Be well.

101
00:12:49,316 --> 00:12:50,727
Vector 137.

102
00:12:50,818 --> 00:12:53,309
Upcoming, Santa Monica Boulevard.

103
00:12:58,534 --> 00:13:00,242
Retina coding accepted.

104
00:13:00,411 --> 00:13:02,487
Warden Smithers, be well.

105
00:13:02,913 --> 00:13:03,992
Go on.

106
00:13:12,089 --> 00:13:13,168
Self-drive on.

107
00:13:13,257 --> 00:13:15,048
Self-drive engaged.

108
00:13:15,425 --> 00:13:16,801
Coding on.

109
00:13:17,094 --> 00:13:20,842
No police presence is requested
in the city at this time.

110
00:13:21,014 --> 00:13:22,177
Report to the station.

111
00:13:22,266 --> 00:13:24,175
Oh, boy, how exciting.

112
00:13:59,928 --> 00:14:00,924
That's it.

113
00:14:01,012 --> 00:14:02,839
"Food, glorious food. "

114
00:14:03,556 --> 00:14:04,967
There'll be another in 12 hours.

115
00:14:05,058 --> 00:14:07,430
These assholes are predictable.

116
00:14:07,811 --> 00:14:09,353
God, I hate this place!

117
00:14:09,437 --> 00:14:11,097
There's not enough of us, Friendly.

118
00:14:11,189 --> 00:14:13,182
That doesn't really matter anymore.

119
00:14:13,274 --> 00:14:14,650
People are hungry.

120
00:14:14,734 --> 00:14:16,643
We've nothing to lose.

121
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:31,828
Greetings.

122
00:14:32,001 --> 00:14:33,543
Lovely Lenina.

123
00:14:35,463 --> 00:14:38,962
Greetings, welcome
to the emergency line of the SAPD.

124
00:14:39,842 --> 00:14:42,843
If you prefer an automated response,
press one now.

125
00:14:43,012 --> 00:14:44,293
Be well.

126
00:14:47,683 --> 00:14:49,676
Mellow greetings, Lenina Huxley.

127
00:14:49,769 --> 00:14:51,761
Let me guess, all is serene?

128
00:14:51,979 --> 00:14:54,766
On the contrary, it's been a horrific a.m.

129
00:14:55,191 --> 00:14:57,349
Public buildings were defaced.

130
00:14:57,526 --> 00:14:59,400
Walls smudged with...

131
00:14:59,862 --> 00:15:01,522
...scandalous graffiti.

132
00:15:01,614 --> 00:15:02,693
Really?

133
00:15:02,865 --> 00:15:05,819
Brutal. Why wasn't there
an "all-cars notify"?

134
00:15:06,035 --> 00:15:09,534
Because there was no need
to create widespread panic.

135
00:15:10,623 --> 00:15:12,366
Lieutenant Huxley...

136
00:15:12,541 --> 00:15:15,542
...I monitored your disheartening
and distressing comments...

137
00:15:15,628 --> 00:15:17,537
...to the warden this morning.

138
00:15:17,630 --> 00:15:20,631
Do you really long for chaos
and disharmony?

139
00:15:21,509 --> 00:15:25,257
Your fascination with the 20th century
is affecting your judgment.

140
00:15:26,222 --> 00:15:30,136
You realize you're setting a bad example
for other officers and personnel.

141
00:15:30,225 --> 00:15:32,895
Thank you for the attitude readjustment.

142
00:15:33,062 --> 00:15:34,770
Info assimilated.

143
00:15:42,571 --> 00:15:44,231
Sanctimonious asshole.

144
00:15:44,406 --> 00:15:47,075
Lenina Huxley, you are fined 1/2 credit...

145
00:15:47,159 --> 00:15:50,243
...for a 'sotto voce' violation
of the verbal-morality statute.

146
00:15:50,329 --> 00:15:51,704
Thank you.

147
00:15:58,754 --> 00:16:00,082
That was tense.

148
00:16:00,422 --> 00:16:02,000
That was tense?

149
00:16:04,092 --> 00:16:08,422
Don't you get bored code tracing perps
who break curfew and tell dirty jokes?

150
00:16:08,889 --> 00:16:10,965
I find my job deeply fulfilling.

151
00:16:11,767 --> 00:16:15,432
I just can't get over the reality
of this office, Lenina.

152
00:16:15,937 --> 00:16:18,393
You're still addicted to the 20th century.

153
00:16:18,482 --> 00:16:21,767
High from its harshness.
Buzzed by its brutality.

154
00:16:22,194 --> 00:16:23,652
Holy smokes!

155
00:16:24,279 --> 00:16:28,526
Is there anything in this office which
doesn't violate Contraband Ordinance 22?

156
00:16:28,617 --> 00:16:29,945
Only you.

157
00:16:31,578 --> 00:16:34,069
Don't you ever want something to happen?

158
00:16:35,290 --> 00:16:36,570
Goodness, no.

159
00:16:37,375 --> 00:16:39,119
I knew you'd say that.

160
00:16:41,963 --> 00:16:44,121
What I wouldn't give for some action.

161
00:16:54,934 --> 00:16:56,678
Mr. Simon Phoenix.

162
00:16:57,896 --> 00:17:00,600
One of our first
and most illustrious members.

163
00:17:01,983 --> 00:17:03,146
Allow me...

164
00:17:03,276 --> 00:17:06,146
